  rankdir="TB";
  "I12" [label="(0,0,0) abduction-reasoning: Observation shows Existing Solutions Gap..., and Knowledge suggests need for expansion..., so Scientific Need defined."];
  "I8" [label="(0,0,0) induction-reasoning: Specifically adding motifs improves..., and Generally protein engineering effective..., so Efficiency Efforts noted."];
  "I9" [label="(0,0,0) induction-reasoning: Specifically two-pegRNA momentum..., and Generally region between nicks..., so Two-pegRNA Context set."];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) This study develops and evaluates EXPERT as a prime-editing system that pairs an upstream cis-acting sgRNA nick with an extended pegRNA to investigate efficient, high-purity editing on both sides of the pegRNA nick, including large-fragment modifications, while addressing directional and range limitations of single-pegRNA and dual-pegRNA prime editors and monitoring low indel and off-target rates.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) The retained and repaired terminal conclusions jointly motivate the paper-level research proposal."];
  "R1" [label="(0,0,0) Prime editing uses a SpyCas9 nickase fused to M-MLV reverse transcriptase together with a pegRNA containing a protospacer and extension as core system components for editing."];
  "R11" [label="(0,0,0) Two-pegRNA approaches have reported limitations, including DSB induction by trans nicks and inability to edit the upstream region."];
  "R12" [label="(0,0,0) Although two-pegRNA approaches have gained attention, their editable region is positioned between downstream nick directions and they retain limitations related to DSB risk and upstream editing."];
  "R13" [label="(0,0,0) A technical gap remains because existing prime-editing approaches are limited by downstream/range constraints, while two-pegRNA strategies also face DSB-risk and upstream-editing limitations."];
  "R16" [label="(0,0,0) The study reports development of EXPERT, a system using an upstream sgRNA for a cis nick together with an extended pegRNA."];
  "R17" [label="(0,0,0) EXPERT is proposed as a design response to the need for expanding prime-editing capability upstream and beyond the narrow downstream range."];
  "R18" [label="(0,0,0) EXPERT is reported to achieve higher product purity than PE2 or twinPE while maintaining low indel rates and minimal off-target effects."];
  "R19" [label="(0,0,0) EXPERT is reported as useful for large-fragment edits and as an effective gene-editing tool."];
  "R2" [label="(0,0,0) The pegRNA component includes a protospacer and a 3' extension, with the extension containing PBS and RTT sequences that encode the intended edit."];
  "R20" [label="(0,0,0) Reported EXPERT performance evidence spans higher product purity, low indel and off-target profiles, and utility for large-fragment editing."];
  "R21" [label="(0,0,0) The EXPERT research idea is motivated by a prime-editing range need and supported by reported design and performance evidence."];
  "R22" [label="(0,0,0) Prior prime-editing improvement efforts include both range-expansion strategies and efficiency-oriented strategies such as adding stabilizing motifs or protein engineering."];
  "R5" [label="(0,0,0) Existing prime editors are described as directionally constrained to downstream editing, with efficient editing above 10% mainly within about 10 bp downstream."];
  "R6" [label="(0,0,0) Cas9 nickase substitution is one reported strategy among efforts to expand the prime-editing range."];
  "R7" [label="(0,0,0) CPE and TJ-PE are examples of other strategies reported to expand prime-editing range and enhance PE performance."];
  "R9" [label="(0,0,0) Prior range-expansion work includes Cas9 nickase substitution as well as CPE and TJ-PE strategies."];
  "S1" [label="(1,0,0) Currently there is PE system constructed by fusing SpyCas9 nickase with M-MLV RT."];
  "S10" [label="(10,0,0) Generally performance of PE has been enhanced through other strategies."];
